title: The Right calls a vote of no confidence against the current government!
subtitle: We have angered our coalition partners too much...
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_rkp = 0
view-if: rsdrp_in_government = 1 and ((in_socialliberal_coalition = 1 or in_popular_front = 1 or in_minority_government = 1) and coalition_dissent >= 3) or (in_trudovaya_coalition = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 4) and rsdrp_r < 50 and not constructive_vonc
tags: event
go-to: vonc_menu

= Vote of No Confidence

[? if in_socialliberal_coalition : The Kadets ?][? if in_trudovaya_coalition or in_popular_front or in_minority_government: The PSR ?] has called for a vote of no confidence against us, due to our various policies and disagreements. If this succeeds, there will be an election in a few months.

@vonc_menu

- @try_assuage: Try to assuage our partners.
- @support_rkp: Could we get the RKP or PLSRI to abstain?
- @let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.

@try_assuage

How do we assuage our partners?

- @austerity: Enact a massive austerity plan and redirect funding to agrarian departments.
- @resources: Use our resources to reduce dissent within the coalition.
- @support_rkp: Could we get the RKP to abstain?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@austerity
view-if: welfare >= 0 and not secularized
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 0; workers_rsdrp -= 10; unemployed_rsdrp -= 10; workers_rkp += 7; workers_nts += 3; unemployed_rkp += 5; unemployed_nts += 5; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent += 5; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; unemployed += 3; rkp_coalition_dissent += 1; rkp_relation -= 10 if in_popular_front

Fine. We enacted a massive austerity program to cut urban welfare while increasing rural funding in order to maintain the stability of our coalition. The vote has been called off.

@resources
view-if: secularized = 0
choose-if: resources >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough resources.
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1;

By transferring resources to our coalition partners, we can reduce their dissent against our policies. This is a crude, but effective solution.

@support_rkp
choose-if: (in_socialliberal_coalition and communist_coalition >= 3 and rkp_relation >= 50 and rkp_r >= kadets_r) or (in_trudovaya_coalition and rkp_relation >= 50 and rkp_r >= psr_r and communist_coalition >= 3)
view-if: tried_supporting_rkp = 0
on-arrival: tried_supporting_rkp = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if communist_coalition < 3 : The RKP won't take part in parliamentary government. ?] [? if rkp_relation < 50 : The RKP is not friendly enough with us. ?] [? if (in_socialliberal_coalition and rkp_r < kadets_r) or (in_trudovaya_coalition and rkp_r < psr_r): The RKP does not have enough votes. ?] [? if in_popular_front : We are already in a Popular Front with the RKP. ?]

If the Communists abstain, then we essentially can maintain a minority government[? if president=="Kornilov":, although it would be very difficult to make policy without the support of President Kornilov, which we do not have ?]. If this happens, then we will own a massive debt to the RKP. This could lead to broader cooperation in the future, for better or for worse.

- @support_rkp_2: Persuade the RKP to "tolerate" us?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@support_rkp_2
on-arrival: communist_coalition += 1; workers_rkp += 3; rkp_relation += 5
go-to: support_rkp_weimar if in_trudovaya_coalition; support_rkp_grand if in_socialliberal_coalition

# TODO: this can form an infinite loop

The RKP is not interested in a "toleration" arrangement; they will only support us if they can participate in the government as part of a coalition. And, if this toleration agreement happens, the right-wing parties will not be inclined to support us. 

@support_rkp_grand

- @election_1928.popular_front_coalition: Form a "Popular Front" coalition?
- @election_1928.left_coalition
- @try_assuage: Never mind. We must deal with this some other way.

@support_rkp_weimar

- @election_1928.left_coalition
- @try_assuage: Never mind. We must deal with this some other way.


@let_it_happen
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; rsdrp_in_government = 0; in_socialliberal_coalition = 0; in_trudovaya_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; rsdrp_toleration = 0; foreign_minister_party = "K-D"; interior_minister_party = "PSR"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "PSR"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = musavat_name; finance_minister_party = "K-D"; agriculture_minister_party = "PSR"; labor_minister = "Kerensky"; interior_minister = "Avksentyev"; finance_minister = "Tereshchenko"; economic_minister = "Jafarov"; justice_minister = "Sorokin"; foreign_minister = "Milyukov"; agriculture_minister = "Chernov"; reichswehr_minister = "Miller";  coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; old_middle_rsdrp -= 3; new_middle_rsdrp -= 2; workers_rsdrp -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; workers_rsdrp -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; old_middle_nts += 4 if pro_republic < 50; new_middle_nts += 3 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: let_it_happen_kornilov if president != "Maisky"; let_it_happen_maisky if president == "Maisky"

@let_it_happen_kornilov
on-arrival: chancellor = "Kerensky"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; welfare -= 2;

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Govenrment-Chairman Kerensky has been appointed as the head of an acting government, consisting solely of Liberal and Narodist parties. He immediately proceeds to direct funding towards rural aims.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@let_it_happen_maisky
on-arrival: rsdrp_caretaker = 1

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] remains as the head of a caretaker government, but no longer has the power to enact new policies.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
